Cozette (vendored)

* What

  Cozette is a 6×13 px bitmap programming font, MIT-licensed,
  upstream at https://github.com/the-moonwitch/Cozette. We use it
  as the default font for the fb-embed dumper / embedding hosts so
  rendered output looks like a real terminal out of the box,
  without contributors having to maintain their own
  ~/.mlterm/font-fb.

* What's here

  cozette.pcf  — runtime artefact, what mlterm actually loads
  LICENSE      — upstream MIT license, unmodified

  We don't ship the upstream .bdf source (~700 KiB) or .otb
  (unused — mlterm's fb backend rejected it). Regen from upstream
  if a newer Cozette release is wanted; see below.

* Pinned version

  v1.30.0  — https://github.com/the-moonwitch/Cozette/releases/tag/v.1.30.0

* How to regenerate cozette.pcf

  Download the .bdf from the upstream release, then run bdftopcf:

    curl -sLO https://github.com/the-moonwitch/Cozette/releases/download/v.1.30.0/cozette.bdf
    bdftopcf cozette.bdf > cozette.pcf
    rm cozette.bdf

  The bdftopcf step emits warnings about Nerd Font private-use
  glyphs (codepoints above U+F0000) being out of PCF's encoding
  range. Those glyphs are skipped silently — the regular ASCII +
  Unicode coverage we actually use is unaffected.
